Description: pause the ticker cooperatively instead of suspend_thread
 The window froze its ticker thread with suspend_thread() while the
 task-entry card was shown ("Time doesn't go when I add a new task"); on
 VOS suspend_thread() has no per-thread form (B_NOT_SUPPORTED). Replace
 the suspend/resume pairs with a shared gTickerPaused flag: the window
 sets it when the card opens and clears it on cancel/OK, and the ticker
 loop skips its one-second tick while it is set. The thread is still
 spawned and resumed once at window construction and is never killed
 (matching upstream, which relies on team teardown).
Author: VitruvianOS Packagers <maintainers@v-os.dev>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/TimeTracker
--- a/src/Defines.h
+++ b/src/Defines.h
@@ -19,4 +19,8 @@
 #define BUTTON_NEW_TASK_OK			3000
 #define BUTTON_NEW_TASK_CANCEL		3001
 
+// Set by the window while the task-entry card is shown; the ticker thread
+// skips its second instead of being suspend_thread()ed (not usable on VOS).
+extern volatile bool gTickerPaused;
+
 #endif
--- a/src/TimeTicker.cpp
+++ b/src/TimeTicker.cpp
